<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base slips 4.94 pct by Feb 21.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base slips 4.94 pct by Feb 21.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base fell 4.94 percent to 2.84 billion sucres in the week to February 21, the Central Bank said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In January 1997, the money base fell 6.8 percent to 2.85 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1996 at 3.06 billion sucres, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
